<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice | David Dindi" description="How personal information should be handled when customers enquire or place orders.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/policies/how-to-order/">Policies</a> / Privacy</div><span class="eyebrow">Customer information</span><h1>Privacy Notice</h1><p class="lead">How personal information should be handled when customers enquire or place orders.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container content">
    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>When this website is connected to contact forms, analytics or messaging services, it may process information such as names, contact details, enquiry contents and basic technical usage data.</p>
    <h2>Purpose and sharing</h2>
    <p>Personal information should be used only for clearly explained business purposes, such as answering enquiries, fulfilling orders, providing support and maintaining website security. Third-party service providers may process data according to their own terms and privacy practices.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
    <p>Provide a monitored contact route for privacy questions or requests relating to personal information. Only collect information that is needed and protect it with appropriate access controls.</p>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Owner/legal review required:</strong> this starter text is not a complete POPIA-compliant privacy notice. Add the responsible party's legal details, actual data flows, purposes, lawful grounds, retention, operators, security measures, rights/request process and any cross-border processing before launch.</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>